<section class="section wrap">
	<h1>Race when you like</h1>
	<p class="lede">The Indoor Racing League is a handicapped Zwift league for Hovélo riders and friends. No start times, no pack racing &mdash; just ride the route whenever suits you, and your time is adjusted for your ability, so anyone can win.</p>
	<div class="actions">
		<a class="button" href="#join">Get involved</a>
		<a class="button button-outline" href="#how">How it works</a>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="band" id="how">
	<div class="wrap">
		<h2>How it works</h2>
		<ol class="steps">
			<li><strong>Ride the qualifier</strong> Ride the league's qualifier route solo and flat out, as many times as you like within the window. Your climb, flat and sprint times become your benchmark.</li>
			<li><strong>Ride each event</strong> Every two weeks there's a new route. Ride it once (or more) whenever suits you between Monday and the Sunday a fortnight later.</li>
			<li><strong>We do the maths</strong> Your time goes up on Strava automatically. We read the club leaderboard, adjust everyone's time against their benchmark, and update the standings.</li>
			<li><strong>Beat yourself, beat everyone</strong> The winner is whoever beats their own prediction by the most. Ride well and your benchmark tightens up a little for next time.</li>
		</ol>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section wrap">
	<h2>The handicap</h2>
	<p>We don't ask for your FTP or weight. Your qualifier ride already tells us how you go on different terrain, compared with the rest of the group:</p>
	<div class="grid grid-3">
		<div class="card">
			<h3>Climbing</h3>
			<p>Your time on the climb segments. Mostly down to watts per kilo.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="card">
			<h3>Flat</h3>
			<p>The rest of the lap. Mostly raw power and how slippery you are.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="card">
			<h3>Sprint</h3>
			<p>Your time on the sprint segments. Short, sharp and painful.</p>
		</div>
	</div>
	<p style="margin-top:1.5rem">Each event is a <span class="badge badge-flat">flat</span>, <span class="badge badge-rolling">rolling</span> or <span class="badge badge-climbing">climbing</span> route, and the handicap leans on whichever ability matters most. Route types rotate so no one body type wins every time.</p>
</section>

<section class="section wrap">
	<h2>Points</h2>
	<div class="grid grid-2">
		<div>
			<h3>Events</h3>
			<ul>
				<li>15 points for the fastest adjusted time, then one fewer per place (never less than 1)</li>
				<li>Plus 2 points every time you finish</li>
				<li>Tied riders share the higher place</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
		<div>
			<h3>Qualifier</h3>
			<ul>
				<li>2 points for riding it</li>
				<li>Bonus 3, 2 and 1 points for the three fastest riders on the full route, the climb and the sprint</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</div>
	<p class="muted">The gaps between places are deliberately small. Turning up always matters.</p>
</section>

<section class="section wrap">
	<h2>The rules</h2>
	<ol>
		<li><strong>Ride solo.</strong> No group rides, races or events &mdash; drafting breaks the handicap.</li>
		<li><strong>Ride the set route, flat out, within the window.</strong> Your best effort counts.</li>
		<li><strong>Keep Zwift's Strava sync switched on</strong> and check your first league ride appears.</li>
		<li><strong>Join the <a href="{{ site.strava }}">Hovélo Strava club</a></strong> so you show up on the leaderboard.</li>
		<li><strong>Don't set rides to "Only You"</strong>, or they won't appear on segment leaderboards.</li>
		<li><strong>Use an honest weight and height in Zwift</strong>, and a smart trainer or power meter if you can.</li>
	</ol>
	<p class="muted">Only initials, adjusted times and points are ever shown. Your raw times stay private.</p>
</section>

<section class="band" id="join">
	<div class="wrap">
		<h2>Get involved</h2>
		<p class="lede">Fancy it? Join the Hovélo Strava club and WhatsApp community, then shout in WhatsApp that you're in. We'll send you the qualifier details.</p>
		<div class="actions">
			<a class="button button-strava" href="{{ site.strava }}">Join the Strava club</a>
			<a class="button button-whatsapp" href="{{ site.whatsapp }}">Join the WhatsApp community</a>
		</div>
		<p class="muted small" style="text-align:center;margin-top:1.5rem">You need to be in the Strava club to show up on the leaderboards.</p>
	</div>
</section>
